---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclosure from '../../components/Disclosure.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../../components/EmailCapture.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
import { goHref, retailerName } from '../../data/affiliate-config';
import saltData from '../../data/salts.json';

interface Salt {
  brand: string;
  product: string;
  gallonsPerBox: number;
  priceUSD: number;
  params: string;
  package: string;
  source: string;
  priceSource: string;
  priceVerifiedOn: string;
  yieldSalinityPpt: number | null;
  yieldNote: string;
  retailers?: string[];
  imageUrl?: string | null;
}
const salts = saltData.salts as Salt[];
// Package yields are reported at different or unknown salinities. Keep source order:
// a numeric price/label-gallon quotient is not a common-35-ppt value ranking.
const withCost = salts.map((s) => ({ ...s, costPerGal: s.priceUSD / s.gallonsPerBox }));
const money = (n: number) => `$${n.toFixed(2)}`;
const examples = [withCost[0], withCost[2], withCost[4]];
const buy = (s: Salt) => goHref(s.retailers || [], `${s.brand} ${s.product} reef salt`, s.priceSource);
const itemListLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ItemList',
  name: 'Reef Salt Mix Package and Salinity Comparison',
  numberOfItems: withCost.length,
  itemListElement: withCost.map((s, i) => ({
    '@type': 'ListItem',
    position: i + 1,
    name: `${s.brand} ${s.product}`,
  })),
};

const headline = "Best reef salt mix: compare package costs and salinity";
---
<Base
  headline={headline}
  title="Best Reef Salt Mix: Packages & Salinity"
  description="Compare 11 reef salt packages, checked prices, chemistry, and yield limits. See why package gallons cannot prove the cheapest salt at 35 ppt."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Reviews', href: '/reviews' }, { name: 'Best Reef Salt Mix', href: '/reviews/best-reef-salt-mix' }]}
>
  <section class="container tool-wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--brand-2)">Reviews · Salt Mix</p>
    <h1>{headline}</h1>
    <p class="lede-dark">Choose a reef salt whose mixed-water chemistry fits the tank you maintain, then compare the exact package and delivered price. A gallon claim at a lower salinity does not buy the same amount of reef water as a gallon at 35 ppt. These listings do not share a verified yield basis, so this page does not name a cheapest-at-35-ppt winner.</p>
    <Disclosure />
    <p class="rnote" style="margin-top:0">Prices and package sizes checked October 25, 2026. Each row links the listing used. The arithmetic below divides that price by the stated package yield; it does not normalize unlike salt mixes. Shipping, tax, sale changes, and retailer stock can change your actual cost. <a href={url('/how-we-rate')}>Full methodology →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="padding-top:8px;padding-bottom:20px;">
    <h2>Three formulas to compare</h2>
    <div class="results">
      {examples.map((s) => (
        <div class="rcard">
          <div class="rmain">
            <div class="rname">{s.brand} {s.product}</div>
            <div class="rmeta">{s.params}</div>
            <div class="rmeta">{s.package} · {money(s.priceUSD)} recorded</div>
            <p class="rmeta">{s.yieldNote}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rbuy"><a class="aff" href={buy(s)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Check price at {retailerName(s.retailers)} (paid link) ↗</a></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="rnote">Use the <a href={url('/tools/salt-cost-calculator')}>salt cost calculator</a> for a package-label spending estimate at your water-change schedule. For a real 35-ppt budget, measure how much water your chosen package makes at your calibrated target salinity.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="padding-top:8px;">
    <h2>All {withCost.length} salt packages — source order, not a value ranking</h2>
    <div class="tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Salt package comparison, scroll for all columns">
      <table class="specs">
        <thead><tr><th>Salt / package</th><th>Recorded price</th><th>Stated yield</th><th>Price / stated gallon</th><th>Yield basis and limits</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {withCost.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{s.brand}</strong> {s.product}<br /><small>{s.package}</small><br /><a href={s.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Formula / yield source</a></td>
              <td>{money(s.priceUSD)}<br /><a href={s.priceSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Price source</a><br /><small>Checked {s.priceVerifiedOn}</small></td>
              <td>{s.gallonsPerBox} US gal</td>
              <td><strong>{money(s.costPerGal)}</strong><br /><small>Package basis only</small></td>
              <td>{s.yieldNote}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="rnote">Fritz illustrates the problem: the maker lists 205 gallons at 30 ppt for its 55-pound box; the retailer calls that box 200 gallons. Mixing to a higher salinity uses more salt per gallon. Other rows have different or unstated yield bases, so the smallest quotient cannot establish the cheapest reef salt.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose" style="padding-top:24px;">
    <h2>Match the fresh mix to the tank</h2>
    <p>Check the maker's alkalinity, calcium, and magnesium targets at the salinity you will use. Coral Pro and standard Red Sea Salt have different listed alkalinity ranges at 35 ppt. Fritz RPM blue and RPM Redline are also different formulas. A familiar brand name is not enough to choose the right product.</p>
    <p>Test a fresh batch before a large change. Water changes can move the tank toward the new water's chemistry; a high-alkalinity salt is not a promise that your corals will grow faster or that dosing is no longer needed. Track consumption with reliable tests and use the <a href={url('/tools/reef-dosing-calculator')}>dosing calculator</a> only with the selected additive's directions.</p>
    <h2>How to compare a real purchase</h2>
    <p>Use the same target salinity, package weight, and final mixed-water volume for each quote. Add delivery and tax. Divide that delivered price by the verified usable gallons at your target, then compare the cost with your water-change schedule. Follow the product's own mixing directions and never add dry salt directly to a stocked tank.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <EmailCapture />
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListLd)} />
</Base>

<style>
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  table.specs { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .92rem; min-width: 560px; }
  table.specs th { text-align: left; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--muted); padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); }
  table.specs td { padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  table.specs tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
</style>
